(ned m21 -- per-fork PUT AWAY from the RACK CAL table.deployed 2026-08-04)
(Pocket N: seat X=#[4100+4N] Y=+1 Ztop=+2 flag=+3. Operator dials #3981)
(load Z and #3982 approach Z AT P1; other forks apply Ztop_N - Ztop_1.)
(Safety framework carried from the live m21: traverse at #3974 0=top,)
(sensor gates around the release, drawbar dwell in clamp/unclamp subs.)
o<m21> sub
#<p> = #1
(FORK COUNT IS #3973, NOT A LITERAL. Operator 2026-08-16 added T15 and)
(could not GET TOOL: the guard below refused pocket 15 outright. #3973 is)
(the count [ATC]POCKETS carries and the GUI reads. Fallback 14 only if the)
(var is unset, which would otherwise refuse EVERY pocket.)
#<nmax> = #3973
o100 if [#<nmax> LT 1]
  #<nmax> = 14
o100 endif
o101 if [[#<p> LT 1] OR [#<p> GT #<nmax>]]
  (abort, m21: pocket #<p> outside 1..#<nmax>)
o101 endif
#<base>  = [4100 + [#<p> * 4]]
o102 if [[#[#<base> + 3] NE 1] OR [ABS[#[#<base> + 2]] LT 0.001]]
  (abort, m21: fork #<p> has no complete RACK CAL data - run RACK CALIBRATION)
o102 endif
o103 if [[#[4107] NE 1] OR [ABS[#[4106]] LT 0.001]]
  (abort, m21: P1 has no RACK CAL data - Z heights are defined relative to P1)
o103 endif
#<sx>  = #[#<base>]
#<sy>  = #[#<base> + 1]
#<dz>  = [#[#<base> + 2] - #[4106]]
#<zload> = [#3981 + #<dz>]
#<zappr> = [#3982 + #<dz>]
(entry clearance: the stowed tool's SAFETY X when set - big tools need a)
(wider berth - else the global clearance offset. #[4200+2T] mirrored from)
(the tool table's SAFETY X column. SAFETY Y is stored and mirrored but not)
(yet consumed: entry on this rack is X-only, and inventing a Y move without)
(an operator-specified direction would guess at which neighbour to avoid.)
#<tnow> = #3991
#<tsx> = 0
o106 if [[#<tnow> GE 1] AND [#<tnow> LE #<nmax>]]
  #<tsx> = #[4200 + [2 * #<tnow>]]
o106 endif
o107 if [#<tsx> GT 0.01]
  #<cx> = [#<sx> - #<tsx>]
o107 else
  #<cx> = [#<sx> + [#3987 - #3983]]
o107 endif
#<ztrav> = #3974
(TRAVERSE RATE IS SET HERE, IN THE FILE, NOT ON THE RACK PAGE. Operator)
(2026-08-16: "i want m6 to go at 80pct of max speed between work and the)
(tool rack" ... "it needs to be something we change on files before we run)
(them. i don't want the production team to be concerned with exact feeds and)
(speeds. that's our job". #3976 is PB's unlabelled ATC USER 3 spare on the)
(rack setup page, so anyone could dial the tool change faster or slower; it)
(is no longer read at all. 80 percent of each axis's OWN ini limit, so this)
(tracks the machine rather than a re-typed number, and Z is not held to X/Y's)
(ceiling nor the reverse.)
(Feed override still applies - operator: "the feed override should touch it".)
(REVERTED TO 0.64 on 2026-08-16. Raising this to 0.80 at 15:11:44 put Z at)
(135 mm/s, and joint 2 following errors followed at 15:13 and 15:53, one of)
(them alongside an rtapi_app SIGSEGV. Correlation, not proof -- but a speed)
(change followed by a servo fault gets reverted before anything else is)
(tried, so the machine returns to a known state. 0.64 is what it ran at)
(before today, via the old #3976 LE 0 fallback.)
#<ftravxy> = #<_ini[axis_x]max_velocity>
o150 if [#<_ini[axis_y]max_velocity> LT #<ftravxy>]
  #<ftravxy> = #<_ini[axis_y]max_velocity>
o150 endif
#<ftravxy> = [0.64 * #<ftravxy> * 60]
#<ftrav>   = [0.64 * #<_ini[axis_z]max_velocity> * 60]
o105 if [#<ztrav> LT #<zappr>]
  (abort, m21: traverse Z is below the approach height for fork #<p>)
o105 endif
M66 P0 L0
o80 if [#5399 LT 1]
  (abort, m21: no tool is clamped - refusing a put-away with an empty spindle)
o80 endif
G90
G1 G53 F[#<ftrav>] Z[#<ztrav>]
G1 G53 F[#<ftravxy>] X[#<cx>] Y[#<sy>]
(SPINDLE GATE. Operator 2026-08-11: "you have to do the check when you get to)
(the unload XY before even descending to the safeZ" -- the old check lived in)
(unload_spindle, which is reached with the tool already down in the fork, so a)
(still-spinning shaft aborted while sitting in the plastic and melted it.)
(M5 first, then WAIT for digital-in-02; abort here, at traverse Z, clear of)
(the rack. Q30 because the spindle coasts down -- there is no brake.)
M5
M66 P2 L3 Q30
o83 if [#5399 LT 0]
  (abort, m21: spindle still turning at the fork XY - NOT descending)
o83 endif
G1 G53 F[#3980] Z[#<zload>]
G4 P1
G1 G53 F[#3980] X[#<sx>]
M24
M66 P1 L0
o81 if [#5399 LT 1]
  (abort, m21: tool-RELEASED never asserted - NOT lifting, tool still gripped)
o81 endif
M66 P0 L0
o82 if [#5399 GT 0]
  (abort, m21: tool-LOCKED still asserted after release - NOT lifting)
o82 endif
(BOOKKEEPING HERE, not in the calling script: the M66 gates above are queue)
(busters, so this point is only reached once the release physically)
(happened. A stop after this line finds every record already true --)
(operator 2026-08-04: "data updated as the atomic actions are completed")
#<was> = #3991
#[4000 + #<p>] = #<was>
#3991 = 0
M61 Q0
G49
(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"rackatc"}.store_tool{#<p>, #<was>}])
(exit lift. operator 2026-08-04: between tools with a PROVEN-empty spindle)
(the full climb to traverse Z is wasted time - lift only to approach+50 and)
(tell m22 via #<_rack_between>. Caller passes #2=1 only when a fetch follows;)
(unload-only paths lift to full traverse Z as before.)
#<fetch_next> = 0
o90 if [EXISTS[#2]]
  #<fetch_next> = #2
o90 endif
o91 if [#<fetch_next> GT 0]
  #<zbetween> = [#<zappr> + 50.0]
  o92 if [#<zbetween> GT 0]
    #<zbetween> = 0
  o92 endif
  #<_rack_between> = 1
  G1 G53 F[#<ftrav>] Z[#<zbetween>]
o91 else
  G1 G53 F[#<ftrav>] Z[#<ztrav>]
o91 endif
o<m21> endsub
M2
